  "title": "Manage Salience Bias",
  "description": "Avoid letting flashy or emotional details overshadow important but less noticeable facts. Here’s how: - Look beyond the obvious: Ask, “What’s not immediately noticeable but might matter?” - Write it down: List both striking and unremarkable details before making decisions. - Weigh all factors: Rank details by importance, not emotional impact. Example: When buying a car, don’t focus only on its color or design—compare safety features and fuel efficiency.",
